# DOE Coal Closure Energy Community Check
# Queries the DOE/NETL 2024 Coal Closure Energy Communities layer.
#
# Input: latitude, longitude
# Output: record with hit (boolean), service name, and feature attributes if found
#
# Usage:
#   devlish run lib/doe_coal_closure.dvl --input '{"latitude": 37.78, "longitude": -81.18}'

inputs:
  latitude
  longitude

query url equals "https://arcgis.netl.doe.gov/server/rest/services/Hosted/2024_Coal_Closure_Energy_Communities/FeatureServer/0/query?geometry=" plus longitude plus "," plus latitude plus "&geometryType=esriGeometryPoint&inSR=4326&spatialRel=esriSpatialRelIntersects&returnGeometry=false&outFields=*&f=json"

Get the url at query url as api response

response body equals body of api response
features equals features of response body

If features is missing:
  Respond with record with false as hit and latitude as latitude and longitude as longitude and "DOECoalClosure" as service

feature count equals count of features

If feature count equals 0:
  Respond with record with false as hit and latitude as latitude and longitude as longitude and "DOECoalClosure" as service

first feature equals first of features
attrs equals attributes of first feature

Respond with record with true as hit and latitude as latitude and longitude as longitude and "DOECoalClosure" as service and attrs as attributes
